 &lt;BR&gt; 
2. The Scheme of Arrangement, Demerger and Reduction of capital filed by the Company and its wholly-owned subsidiary Robust Hotels Private Limited, Chennai (Robust) have been sanctioned by the Hon'ble NCLT Chennai Bench and NCLT Kolkata Bench vide orders dated 13th October, 2021 and 20th December, 2021 respectively. The said Scheme will be effective on filing the same with the respective Registrar of Companies, which is under process and the effect of the scheme is expected to be given upon its filing in the upcoming quarters and thereupon Robust will cease to exist as a wholly-owned subsidiary of the Company. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
3. Exceptional items represent gain on sale of 100% shares of Regency Convention Centre &amp; Hotels Ltd (RCC) to Mumbai International Airport Ltd. (MIAL). RCC has ceased to be a wholly-owned subsidiary of the Company. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
4. The Company has significant strategic investments in the equity shares of Asian Hotels (West) Limited (AHWL). The market price of shares of AHWL has fallen considerably since the sudden closure of Hyatt Regency Mumbai Hotel effective from 7th June 2021 by its management due to various non-compliance issues. The Company expects a further substantial fall in the market value of shares till AHWL resumes its operations. The Company has filed Oppression &amp; Mismanagement petitions under section 241-242 &amp; 244 of the Companies Act, 2013 with the  NCLT Principal Bench, New Delhi in order to protect its interest. Financial lenders have initiated CIRP resolution under section 7 of IBC, 2016 against AHWL. The Company has taken necessary steps in this regard to protect its interest. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
5. As per direction of Governement of Odisha, the Company has provided Performance Bank Guarantee from IDBI Bank of Rs 3,500 lakhs to the Government for setting up of a Hotel in Bhubaneshwar on behalf of its wholly-owned subsidiary, GJS Hotels Ltd. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
